shortdesc Montserrat sans serif, otf and pfb, with LaTeX support files
relocated 1
longdesc Montserrat is a geometric sans-serif typeface designed by
longdesc Julieta Ulanovsky, inspired by posters and signage from her
longdesc historical Buenos Aires neighborhood of the same name. It is
longdesc rather close in spirit to Gotham and Proxima Nova, but has its
longdesc own individual appearance -- more informal, less extended, and
longdesc more idiosyncratic. It is provided in a total of nine different
longdesc weights, each having eight figure styles and small caps in both
longdesc upright and italic shapes. There are two quite different
longdesc versions that don't fit into the usual LaTeX classifications.
longdesc The version having the appellation "Alternates" has letter
longdesc shapes that are much more rounded than the default version,
longdesc reflecting the signage in the neighborhood of Montserrat.
